# Architecture Document
  
## Context
An industrial organization operates many ML models across plants and environments. The platform provides a central system to register, version, approve, deploy, monitor, and roll back machine-learning models, with a focus on governance and operational reliability rather than model training.

## Scope
This document covers the MLOps Model Registry and Deployment Management platform. The current implementation is a vertical slice covering model registration, versioning, lifecycle governance, deployment with idempotency, retry, rollback, and a web-based operational UI.

## Architecture Overview
  The system follows a layered architecture with clear separation of concerns:
  Presentation Layer: HTML/JavaScript frontend (proof of concept; production target is Angular with TypeScript, Angular Material, and RxJS)
  API Layer: Python/FastAPI REST backend with typed request/response models, input validation, and auto-generated OpenAPI documentation
  Domain Layer: Business logic for lifecycle governance (approval gates), deployment state management, idempotency, retry, and rollback
  Persistence Layer: Currently in-memory storage; production target is SQLAlchemy with PostgreSQL/SQLite and Alembic migrations
    
